body: "## Hosted CI defect\n\nAt [PR #64](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ado/pull/64) head `1873ac06cf97a98e224d0e8fabd024f05c652eb6`, the four test/release jobs in run 42163459633 fail at the generated changelog check. The head, discussion and latest checks were rechecked on 2026-11-06; no newer successful run supersedes these failures.\n\nThe inspected checkout is synthetic merge `85e475a700e3c430de48cf7503934005a559184d`, merging that candidate into base `0b3d5a38611ae00dd375393d7f9133249783ebf9`. Package version is `2026.11.5`; the declared pm-changelog pin is `2026.10.31`. PR #64 changes only the CodeQL workflow. This report does not attribute the failure to that action update.\n\n## Evidence and exact failure\n\nFull official logs inspected:\n- [Node 26](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ado/actions/runs/42163459633/job/127714311203)\n- [npm release gate](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ado/actions/runs/42163459633/job/127714311246)\n- [Bun release gate](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ado/actions/runs/42163459633/job/127714311252)\n\nEach reaches `changelog:check` after passing coverage, production audit and package packing. Coverage reports 1,095/1,095 tests passing, zero failures, and 2,351/2,351 independently measured statements at the unchanged 100% statement gate. Production audits report zero vulnerabilities.\n\nAll three then exit 1 with this same committed-versus-generated difference:\n\n```diff\n # Changelog\n \n+## Unreleased\n+\n+No changes.\n+\n ## 2026.11.5 - 2026-11-05\n \n No changes.\n```\n\n[Node 22 step results](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ado/actions/runs/42163459633/job/127714310878) independently confirm successful coverage/audit/packing followed by changelog failure; its full log was not separately inspected.\n\nThe [committed changelog](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ado/blob/1873ac06cf97a98e224d0e8fabd024f05c652eb6/CHANGELOG.md#L1-L7) begins with the dated release. The [package scripts](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ado/blob/1873ac06cf97a98e224d0e8fabd024f05c652eb6/package.json#L39-L45) use replacement/all-release-tags/include-empty generation for both `changelog:full` and `changelog:check`, with `--check` added for validation.\n\n## Expected, impact and limits\n\nThe established [canonical changelog goal](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ado/blob/0b3d5a38611ae00dd375393d7f9133249783ebf9/.agents/pm/issues/pm-ado-r5ps.toon) and [PR #74](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ado/pull/74) require generation and checking to agree while preserving truthful empty dated releases. On the observed source and fetched-tag context, validation instead requires an additional empty pending section. This blocks the complete CI/release gate.\n\nThis is a hosted artifact-consistency finding, not a locally reproduced generator root cause or an Azure/native-backend runtime regression. No new tests, installs, provider calls, reruns, merges or releases were performed for this review. Changes in tag context versus generation-time state remain to be isolated rather than assumed.\n\nLater publish-attestation, release-date and native-precondition checks were skipped or not reached after the failure. Passing the preceding tests does not certify the full release gate or native-precondition conformance.\n\n## Acceptance and regression criteria\n\n- Reconcile generated and committed changelog semantics so the standard check passes deterministically for the same source and explicit release/tag context, without an unexplained empty-heading diff.\n- Add a focused regression covering a prepared empty dated release and subsequent post-tag validation, plus a genuine pending change. Preserve truthful dated `No changes.` sections and real unreleased entries.\n- Keep generation centralized in the existing package scripts. Do not bypass the check, suppress meaningful changes or weaken coverage/release gates.\n- Rerun Node 22/26 and npm/Bun gates on one immutable corrected head, showing the changelog check and previously unreached later stages separately.\n\n## Deduplication\n\nChecked all 89 all-status ADO issue/PR records, current PR #64 discussion, related #71/#74/#89 discussions and all 51 canonical records at the current default (each verified against its Git blob hash). No exact owner for this failure was found. Closed `pm-ado-r5ps`/#74 addressed an earlier duplicated-workflow-flags mismatch; [pm-changelog #47](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/issues/47) describes older stale/duplicated Unreleased behavior. Neither establishes that this distinct current ADO failure is already tracked.\n\n\n---\n\n### GitHub comments (1)\n\n> **@coderabbitai[bot]** (2026-11-06T05:37:58Z)\n>\n> <!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n> \n> <!-- This is an auto-generated issue plan by CodeRabbit -->\n> <details>\n> <summary>🔗 Related PRs</summary>\n> <dl>\n> <dd>\n> <br>\n> \n> unbraind/pm-ado#74 - Generate the release changelog only through the package scripts [merged]\n> </dd>\n> </dl>\n> </details>\n> \n> ---\n> <details>\n> <summary>📝 Issue Planner</summary>\n> <dl>\n> <dd>\n> <br>\n> \n> <sub>Check the box below or use the `@coderabbitai plan` command to generate an implementation plan and prompts that you can use with your favorite coding assistant.</sub>\n> \n> - [ ] <!-- {\"checkboxId\":\"8d4f2b9c-3e1a-4f7c-a9b2-d5e8f1c4a7b9\"} --> Create Plan\n> </dd>\n> </dl>\n> </details>\n> \n> \n> ---\n> <details>\n> <summary> 🧪 Issue enrichment is currently in open beta.</summary>\n> <dl>\n> <dd>\n> <br>\n> \n> \n> You can configure auto-planning by selecting labels in the issue_enrichment configuration.\n> \n> To disable automatic issue enrichment, add the following to your `.coderabbit.yaml`:\n> ```yaml\n> issue_enrichment:\n>   auto_enrich:\n>     enabled: false\n> ```\n> </dd>\n> </dl>\n> </details>\n> \n> 💬 Have feedback or questions? Drop into our [discord](https://discord.gg/coderabbit)!"
